{"id": "unknown-2026-09-04-014", "date": "2026-09-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South India cotton yarn turns soft amid falling cotton prices", "content": "Mumbai cotton yarn sentiment weakened as falling cotton prices, sluggish downstream demand and payment constraints weighed on buying, with carded yarn easing by ₹3–5 per kg.\nTiruppur cotton yarn prices stayed largely steady, though sellers offered higher discounts after recent price rises.\nGujarat cotton retreated as a sharp fall in ICE cotton futures dampened demand.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/south-india-cotton-yarn-turns-soft-amid-falling-cotton-prices-313238-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-04-015", "date": "2026-09-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India GeM, Textiles Committee sign MoU to support circular textiles", "content": "GeM and the Textiles Committee have signed an MoU to route recycled and upcycled textile products into Indian public procurement.\nThe tie-up targets goods made from pre- and post-consumer waste, scrap and second-hand clothes.\nDedicated GeM categories, certification and handholding may open demand for MSMEs, artisans and recyclers.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-gem-textiles-committee-sign-mou-to-support-circular-textiles-313231-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-04-016", "date": "2026-09-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["plunge"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "US Upland cotton sales plunge 71%, shipment rise 4.7%: USDA", "content": "US Upland cotton net sales for 2026-27 fell about 71 per cent week on week to 27,500 RB, with India and Vietnam the largest buyers at 10,800 RB each. \nUpland shipments rose about 4.7 per cent to 189,500 RB, led by Vietnam at 77,300 RB and India at 22,200 RB. \nPima sales slipped about 14 per cent to 1,800 RB, while shipments fell about 47 per cent to 4,600 RB. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/us-upland-cotton-sales-plunge-71-shipment-rise-4-7-usda-313229-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
